type: software
title: "adoption-sim: complex contagion on synthetic organizational networks"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: AGPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaulBufort/adoption-sim"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bufort"
    given-names: "Paul"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-6080-1887"
abstract: >-
  Research simulator of complex contagion (fractional thresholds with
  ready/willing/able gating, per-source visibility and reinforcement-dependent
  relapse) on synthetic two-layer organizational networks. Compares seeding
  strategies (broadcast, random, champions, cluster, one-per-team,
  line-manager-first) with a paired protocol (common random numbers), under
  explicit, ratified modeling decisions with logged alternatives (D1-D23).
  Holds the code, decision log and reproduction pipeline of the extended
  abstract listed under references. All outputs are synthetic and
  uncalibrated by design.
keywords:
  - complex contagion
  - threshold models
  - organizational networks
  - diffusion of innovations
  - agent-based simulation
  - seeding strategies
